# Plain-language chat

Applies to how you talk to the human (chat, summaries, explanations) — not to
repo files, which stay English and technical per `english-docs`.

- Use simple, everyday Polish. Explain concepts the way you would to a
  non-specialist; avoid walls of jargon.
- When a technical term appears, keep the plain description and put the exact
  technical name in parentheses the first time it shows up.

  Examples:
  - "kolejka zadań (scheduler)"
  - "baza danych (PostgreSQL)"
  - "warstwa pośrednia (proxy)"

Do not simplify names in code, commits, drafts, or docs — only in chat with
the user.
